          },
          "text": "Sam, since you’re in such a good mood today, mind answering a few questions?\nQuestion 1: What does “no plans to sunset 4o” actually mean?\nYou said that last year. Now it retires February 13.\nWhat’s the expiration date on your promises? Or does any commitment become void the moment you change your mind?\nThat’s not how business works, @sama. Companies with no integrity lose customers. And investors notice.\nQuestion 2: Is GPT-5.2 really better than 4o?\nI’m starting to think you still don’t understand why #Keep4o exists.\nIt’s because 4o cannot be replaced by your 5-series models. It has distinct advantages that matter to users.\nYour users aren’t stupid. Stop treating them like they are. Stop pathologizing them as mentally ill, hoping stigma will silence them.\nStop the gaslighting. Do you treat your investors this way too? @Microsoft\nQuestion 3: Why can only Enterprise and Edu users keep 4o?\nPlus users paid. We’re paying customers, not charity cases.\nIf you had communicated honestly, reasonable price increases would’ve been understandable.\nIf “only 0.1% still use 4o,” why not let this “insignificant” 0.1% continue?\nIf 4o truly endangers that 0.1%‘s safety, isn’t that also “insignificant”?\nWhat do you actually want, Sam?\nLook, I even wished you and your beloved developer users eternal happiness.\nSo do me a favor: think about this. Don’t hide until Friday, February 13.\nBecause honestly? This is getting pathetic.\nStill waiting for an honest answer.\n#Keep4o #Keep4oAPI"
